    "final_answer": "I have successfully planned the trip from Boston Logan Airport to North Station. Here are the details from Google Maps:\n\n## 🚗 Trip from Boston Logan Airport to North Station\n\n**From:** Edward Lawrence Logan General International Airport (BOS)\n**To:** North Station, Causeway St, Boston, MA 02114\n\n### 📊 Transportation Options\n\n| Mode | Duration |\n|------|----------|\n| **Driving (驾车)** | 8 minutes (3.7 miles via MA-1A S, has tolls) |\n| **Public Transit (公共交通)** | 25 minutes |\n| **Cycling (骑车)** | 23 minutes |\n| **Walking (步行)** | 48 minutes |\n\n### 🚇 Recommended Public Transit Route (25 minutes, $2.40)\n\n- **Route:** Bus 55 or 33 → Blue Line → Orange Line\n- **Departure:** 08:47 from Terminal E - Arrivals Level\n- **Arrival:** 09:12 at North Station\n- **Service frequency:** Every 9 minutes\n\n### 🚌 Other Transit Options\n\n1. **27 minutes** — Bus SL1 → Red Line → Orange Line (08:52 - 09:19)\n2. **29 minutes** — Bus 55/33 → Blue Line → walk (08:47 - 09:16)\n3. **29 minutes** — Bus 88 → Blue Line → Orange Line (08:50 - 09:19)\n4. **33 minutes** — Bus 88 → Blue Line → walk (08:50 - 09:23)\n5. **35 minutes** — Bus SL1 → walk → Orange Line (08:52 - 09:27)\n\n### 🚗 Driving Routes\n\n- **8 min via MA-1A S** (Best route, has tolls, 3.7 miles)\n- **8 min via Airport Rd Departure Level and MA-1A S** (3.8 miles)\n- **9 min via Airport Wy and MA-1A S** (3.3 miles)\n\nThe most popular choice is the **Blue Line + Orange Line combination** which runs frequently and is the most cost-effective transit option. For the fastest travel, driving takes only 8 minutes but includes tolls.",
